A||||4||Dan86gt3.8||Does anyone know how to get the ground effects off?||||5||
Z||000000||Dan86gt3.8||06-13-2000||11:19 PM||||Well guys its repaint time.  We started sanding on her today.  But first I need to get the gt side windows out.  They are already spyder cracked and cracked via my dad leaning on it topnight so theres no worry about cracking them.  Also I need to take off the lower ground effects on both sides.  It looks like it is attached somehow to the bottom of the door jam.  Anywho please reply or link me to a site with the instructions.  thanks in advance!||||reg||5
Z||000001||TOM||06-13-2000||11:52 PM||||big pull rivets. and the upper ones are held on the doors etc with nuts.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Spyder||06-14-2000||12:10 AM||||From what I remember the ground effects do use the big plastic rivets, what I used to remove them was a chisel and hammer. On the side glass there is a bolt that is accessible only  from inside of the car.||||reg||1
Z||000003||My7Fieros||06-14-2000||01:40 AM||||I believe the fastback quarter windows are only held on by some SUPER DUPER strong adhesive tape...use a wire to pull behind the window to cut through the tape. I actually saw some wire made just for jobs like that today in the automotive paint store. I dont believe (but I may be wrong)that there is a bolt holding on the fastback windows...only the 84-87 notchbacks..(the 88 notchbacks, mine at least, has adhesive and ha strange hook thing..hmmm)<BR>My 0.02 worth plus 8.25% Tennessee sales tax  ;-)||||reg||1
Z||000004||bHooper||06-14-2000||07:41 AM||||actually, i found that the ground efx were held in place with a few plastic fastners as well as those 1/4" aluminum pull rivits.  when reataching those, you will need a hd rivit gun... no snap rivit gun, here.  you can get them from fiero store, but i also think that George has them.||||reg||1
